BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Adam de Boer in Conversation with Christine Cocca
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260812
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260813
DTSTAMP:20260812T112646Z
UID:12309c558bc886dd6a314a60b2f0@visitri-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Artist Talk: After the Fire: Batik\, Memory\, and the Lives Tr
 ees Hold RSVP encouraged |Pay-what-you-can Join artist Adam de Boer for a 
 lively\, illustrated conversation with Jamestown Arts Center Executive Dir
 ector Christine Cocca on the occasion of A Celebration of Trees. Rather th
 an a traditional artist lecture\, this evening will unfold as a dialogue b
 etween de Boer and Cocca\, whose shared experiences as Fulbright scholars 
 in Yogyakarta\, Indonesia\, provide a natural point of connection for a br
 oader conversation about art\, place\, cultural exchange\, and the ways la
 ndscapes shape creative practice. Beginning with de Boer’s Reconstructio
 n Site No. 5\, currently on view in the exhibition\, the conversation will
  consider how trees\, coastlines\, cityscapes\, and sites of destruction a
 nd renewal can hold memory\, identity\, and transformation. In January 202
 5\, the Los Angeles wildfires devastated de Boer’s neighborhood of Altad
 ena. As the son of a firefighter\, de Boer had long understood fire as par
 t of California’s ecological and cultural reality\, but experiencing the
  disaster so closely reshaped his relationship to the place he calls home.
  His ongoing Reconstruction Site series records not only destruction\, but
  also endurance\, renewal\, and the intimate ways a city begins to rebuild
  after loss. The discussion will also trace de Boer’s long engagement wi
 th Javanese batik\, a centuries-old textile tradition that he has adapted 
 into a hybrid painting practice. Through images\, process documentation\, 
 and exchange\, de Boer and Cocca will discuss molten beeswax\, canting too
 ls\, staining\, boiling\, oil painting\, and the deeper questions embedded
  in technique: what it means to inherit\, translate\, and transform a cult
 ural form across geographies. Together\, they will reflect on California a
 nd Indonesia\, wildfire and memory\, Dutch-Indonesian heritage\, and the r
 ole of artistic practice in making sense of the places that form us. The e
 vening will include projected images\, behind-the-scenes views of de Boer
 ’s process\, and time for audience Q&amp\;A. About the Artist Adam de Bo
 er is a Los Angeles-based artist whose work combines traditional Javanese 
 crafts\, including batik and wood carving\, with Western oil painting as a
  way to connect his artistic practice with those of his distant cultural f
 orebears. For more than a decade\, his coastal scenes\, cityscapes\, and a
 rchitectural landscapes have explored the visual textures\, cultural mingl
 ings\, and socioeconomic realities of California and Indonesia. His recent
  work depicts the cultural hodgepodge of Los Angeles while maintaining a s
 trong connection to his Dutch-Indonesian immigrant heritage. De Boer recei
 ved a BFA in Painting from the College of Creative Studies at the Universi
 ty of California\, Santa Barbara\, and an MA in Fine Art from Chelsea Coll
 ege of Arts\, University of the Arts London. His work has been exhibited i
 nternationally\, including at Jane Lombard Gallery\, New York\; Gazelli Ar
 t House\, London\; Plato\, New York\; Taymour Grahne Projects\, London\; T
 he Pit\, Los Angeles\; Gajah Gallery\, Jakarta and Singapore\; Ben Brown F
 ine Arts\, London and Hong Kong\; The Hole\, New York and Los Angeles\; Wo
 rld Trade Centre\, Jakarta\; and Art Jog\, Yogyakarta. De Boer is a Joan M
 itchell Foundation Fellowship alumnus and\, in 2017\, was awarded a Fulbri
 ght Research Fellowship to Java\, Indonesia. His additional grants and awa
 rds include the International Art Prize presented by Winsor &amp\; Newton 
 and Paul Smith’s Foundation\, and Arts for India from the University of 
 the Arts London.\n\nSource: https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/adam-de
 -boer-in-conversation-with-christine-cocca/111252/
LOCATION:Jamestown Arts Center\, 18 Valley Street\, Jamestown\, 02835
URL:https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/adam-de-boer-in-conversation-wi
 th-christine-cocca/111252/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Aurora Skies - Painting Class
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260812
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260813
DTSTAMP:20260812T112646Z
UID:d88bb7f6bfee0a85bcca1879229e@visitri-calendar
DESCRIPTION:🖌️ IN-STUDIO SESSION DETAILS Reserve your spot and enjoy 
 a complimentary beverage—choose from soda\, beer\, or wine (21+ with val
 id ID). Additional drinks will be available for purchase. Immerse yourself
  in a fun and creative atmosphere while painting your own unique masterpie
 ce! Recommended for ages 14 and up. ⏰ ARRIVAL TIME Our studio opens 30 m
 inutes prior to class time. We recommend arriving 15&#8211\;30 minutes ear
 ly to find parking\, grab a drink\, and get settled. Please note: If you a
 rrive late\, the artist may not be able to fill you in on the steps you mi
 ssed\, as they will be focused on guiding the rest of the class. If you ar
 rive more than 20 minutes late\, we kindly ask that you do not join the se
 ssion. Late arrivals can be disruptive and may not have enough time to com
 plete the painting. Unfortunately\, we cannot offer refunds or reschedules
  for late arrivals. 🚗 PARKING INFO Our studio is located at 150 Main St
 reet (rear entrance)\, Pawtucket\, Rhode Island\, and we have two FREE par
 king lots: 🚗 One directly attached to our entrance 🚗 A second lot ju
 st one building down on the same side of the street — clearly labeled 
 🪑 WANT TO SIT WITH FRIENDS? If you purchased 2 or more tickets in one t
 ransaction\, we’ll automatically seat your group together. If you booked
  separately but want to sit with someone\, please include their first and 
 last names in the “Additional Information / Order Notes” field during 
 checkout. 🔄 RESCHEDULING &amp\; CANCELLATION POLICY All reservations ar
 e non-refundable. However\, if you need to reschedule\, you may request a 
 reschedule voucher at least 48 hours before your session. You can do this 
 easily on our website — just [click here]. No-shows cannot be reschedule
 d. 🚨 CLASS CANCELLATION Classes may be canceled due to low attendance. 
 In this case\, we’ll notify you and issue a voucher for a future session
 . We appreciate your understanding and look forward to welcoming you to a 
 future class! ❄️ INCLEMENT WEATHER POLICY Because New England weather 
 can be unpredictable\, we typically wait until a few hours before class to
  make final decisions. If we cancel due to snow or other severe weather\, 
 we’ll email you a voucher for a future session. Have more questions? Che
 ck out our [Frequently Asked Questions] page — just [click here].\n\nSou
 rce: https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/aurora-skies-painting-class/11
 0937/
LOCATION:Paint and Vino\, 150 Main Street\, Pawtucket\, RI 02860
URL:https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/aurora-skies-painting-class/110
 937/
END:VEVENT
