BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Teacher's Lounge
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260812
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260813
DTSTAMP:20260812T112646Z
UID:f53fa7b72085f05c102d35e78cf3@visitri-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Join three seasoned educators—Gaspare Randazzo (Netflix\, Th
 e Social Studies Podcast and @StandUpRandazzo on social media)\, Philip Li
 ndsay (Social Media Sensation @Mr_PhLindsay_Sped on IG\, The Today Show)\,
  and Andrea Forcum (How To Survive The Classroom Podcast and @EducatorAndr
 ea on TikTok)—for a hilarious inside look at the unpredictable\, often a
 bsurd world of teaching in The Teacher’s Lounge. This live show is packe
 d with laugh-out-loud stories from the classroom\, outrageous Q&amp\;A ses
 sions\, and an unfiltered celebration of the highs and lows of the profess
 ion. Whether you're a teacher or just curious about what really happens at
  school\, this show promises to entertain and offer a fresh perspective yo
 u won't want to miss!\n\nSource: https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/te
 achers-lounge/111067/
LOCATION:Comedy Connection\, 39 Warren Avenue\, East Providence\, RI 02914
URL:https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/teachers-lounge/111067/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Washington County Fair
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260812
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260813
DTSTAMP:20260812T112646Z
UID:e9349cbadfa54061b73d240ec35b@visitri-calendar
DESCRIPTION:The Fair is RI's largest agricultural event. Admission include
 s access to all daily concerts\, special acts and events\, the giant midwa
 y and kiddy land area (all ride tickets &amp\; games separate)\, agricultu
 ral events/shows\, exhibits/displays\, tractor and horse pulls\, farm muse
 um\, and much more! At the Main Stage pine grove you can relax and enjoy s
 ome of music's hottest acts...one of the biggest draws to the Fair is toda
 y's Country Music Stars! Bring the entire family for five full days of FUN
 !\n\nSource: https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/washington-county-fair
 /110326/
LOCATION:Washington County Fairgrounds\, 78 Richmond Townhouse Road\, Rich
 mond\, RI 02812
URL:https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/washington-county-fair/110326/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:"Mea Duke: Dreamliners" Exhibit
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260813
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260814
DTSTAMP:20260812T112646Z
UID:d4e7b3cf0b2067165006c2948d8a@visitri-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Jessica Hagen Fine Art + Design is pleased to announce the exh
 ibit: "Mea Duke: Dreamliners" August 1 - August 30\, 2026. This solo exhib
 ition marks Mea Duke’s third solo show with Jessica Hagen’s gallery. D
 reamliners assembles objects and images from the mid-twentieth century mom
 ent when progress felt most like destiny: Pan Am flying boats\, LIFE magaz
 ines\, lifejackets\, sunblock\, straw hats\, shipping containers\, endless
  horizons. Together they form an archive of optimism\, sleek engineering\,
  and the promise that the world was suddenly\, thrillingly within reach. T
 he title borrows from Boeing's Dreamliner\, an aircraft whose name still t
 rades on the same aspirational language the Pan Am era perfected. Duke's p
 ractice has long lived in the space between painting an object and treatin
 g the painting itself as an object\, an artifact with its own weight\, mat
 eriality\, and history. Jessica Hagen states\, “Dreamliners is a smart\,
  fun and beautifully executed show. Mea Duke is a highly skilled painter a
 nd she is very clearly on top of her game\; treating us to paintings that 
 are in her words\, created slowly by hand\, with clean deliberate precisio
 n. Replete with iconic objects and imagery rendered as only Duke can\, thi
 s show is not to be missed.” “Mea Duke: Dreamliners” closes August 3
 0\, 2026. Jessica Hagen Fine Art + Design was founded in 2005 and features
  contemporary art including painting\, sculpture\, photography\, ceramics\
 , textiles\, and jewelry. Located in the historic Point section of Newport
 \, the gallery’s hours are Wednesday- Saturday 11:00 AM - 5:00 PM\, and 
 Sunday 12:00 - 5:00 PM. The gallery is also open by appointment. Image Att
 ached: Mea Duke Flying Boat I oil/canvas 40” x 64”\n\nSource: https://
 www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/mea-duke%3a-dreamliners-exhibit/111171/
LOCATION:Jessica Hagen Fine Art & Design\, 9A Bridge Street\, Newport\, RI
  02840
URL:https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/mea-duke%3a-dreamliners-exhibit
 /111171/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Early Bird Museum Highlight Tour at Newport Car Museum
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260813
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260814
DTSTAMP:20260812T112646Z
UID:3bc98d69aef3bc53313af54b2d21@visitri-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Early Bird Highlight Tour For 90 minutes (8:30 &#8211\; 10:00 
 AM) prior to Museum opening. Call to book: +1 (401) 848-2277 Price $75.00 
 per person (minimum 2\, maximum 6 ppl) Offered Wednesday\, Thursday\, and 
 Saturday only April 1 - December 31\, 2026. General admission is included 
 with price. 72-hour advance notice is suggested. Only one group will be ho
 sted on any given morning. This is your chance to have the Newport Car Mus
 eum all to yourself with a private guide to share with you the not-to-miss
  highlights in seven expansive galleries. With over 100 iconic\, rare and 
 exotic cars on display at one time\, this private collection is bursting w
 ith history\, provenance and color\, not to mention the breathtaking sculp
 tural beauty of automotive designs starting with the 1950s and finishing w
 ith new models from the 21 st Century. After 90 minutes with your private\
 , continue to explore at your own pace so that you can further examine you
 r favorites from the Ford/Shelby\, Corvette\, World Car\, Porsche\, Fin Ca
 r\, American Muscle and Mopar exhibits while enjoying immersive videos\, a
 rtwork and the Museum’s eclectic collection of Mid-Century Modern Furnit
 ure.\n\nSource: https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/early-bird-museum-h
 ighlight-tour-at-newport-car-museum/109638/
LOCATION:Newport Car Museum\, Enter at Light 1947 West Main Road\, Portsmo
 uth\, RI 02871
URL:https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/early-bird-museum-highlight-tou
 r-at-newport-car-museum/109638/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
